# Walkthrough: Email Watcher Debugging

I addressed the issue where the IT Inventory system was not processing email requests.

## Changes Made

### Configuration Updates
- **Removed Sender Filter**: Cleared `WATCH_SENDER_FILTER` in [.env](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/it-inventory/.env) to allow scanning emails from any sender to the `it@findtalent.net` mailbox.
- **Set Direct Server**: Configured `EXCHANGE_SERVER=outlook.office365.com` to bypass autodiscover issues.
- **Improved Scripting**: Created [debug_exchange.py](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/it-inventory/inventory_app/debug_exchange.py) for standalone testing and better logging.

## Verification Results

### Web Interface
The dashboard is successfully running and accessible at [http://localhost:8001](http://localhost:8001).

### Email Watcher Status
> [!IMPORTANT]
> The background service is currently failing to connect to Exchange due to **Invalid Credentials**.

**Current Log Status:**
`it-inventory | 2026-03-25 06:52:18,642 - ERROR - Exchange bağlantı hatası: Invalid credentials for https://outlook.office365.com/EWS/Exchange.asmx`

### Next Steps for the User
- **Verify Password**: Please double-check if `Eralp123!` is the current password for `it@findtalent.net`.
- **App Password**: If 2-Factor Authentication is enabled on the account, you must generate an **App Password** from your Microsoft account settings and use it in the [.env](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/it-inventory/.env) file.
- **Restart**: After updating the password in [.env](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/it-inventory/.env), run `docker compose up -d` to apply changes.
